.TH ZHEN\-FLYWHEEL 1 "2026-10-29" "unheaded 6b26b19a" "Unheaded Kingdom"
.SH NAME
zhen\-flywheel \- Turn training captures into labelled, filtered, held\-out training data (wiki/Zhen\-Training\-Data.md).
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zhen\-flywheel
COMMAND [OPTION]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Turn training captures into labelled, filtered, held\-out training data (wiki/Zhen\-Training\-Data.md).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B ingest [\-dir DIR]
capture files to the Well (strict, re\-scanned, deduped)
.TP
.B label
outcomes to labels (checks, escalations, reviews, judges, edits)
.TP
.B export \-out DIR
the Well to SFT, preference and tool\-trace files, split and tokenized
.TP
.B scan DIR
secret/PII re\-scan of an export (exit 1 on any finding)
.TP
.B quarantine CAPTURE\-ID
mark one capture for the purge
.TP
.B import\-eval \-results FILE \-answers\-dir DIR
kept eval answers to capture files
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
display this help and exit
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
output version information and exit
.SH NOTES
WELL_APP_ZHEN_DSN (unheaded_app as app_zhen) is required by ingest, label, export and quarantine; WELL_OPS_DSN (unheaded_ops) is optional for label. Neither has a default: credentials are never in the repository.
Claude\-authored text never leaves export unless \-include\-claude\-text (or ZHEN_FLYWHEEL_INCLUDE_CLAUDE_TEXT=1) is given.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR unheaded (1)
